    <!--
    quarkus.bootstrap.effective-model-builder=true was tried here to fix a real, documented Quarkus
    bug (quarkusio/quarkus#7747): Quarkus's bootstrap resolver re-reads any Maven-reactor sibling's
    raw pom.xml without property interpolation, so a sibling using CI-friendly ${revision}
    versioning (forwardmeasure-jpa, built as a reactor.xml module alongside this repo) fails with
    the literal string "${revision}" being resolved as a real Maven coordinate. Reverted: enabling
    it trades that bug for a different, genuine Quarkus bug - confirmed via a full stack trace, not
    guessed - io.quarkus.bootstrap.resolver.maven.workspace.WorkspaceLoader.findVersions calls
    List.of(a, b) with a null element while importing a <dependencyManagement> BOM for another
    reactor sibling's (forwardmeasure-entity-intelligence) effective model, and List.of() rejects
    nulls outright. Net loss, not a fix, for this reactor's composition. Left disabled until either
    Quarkus fixes that null-handling bug or a different workaround (e.g. building ${revision}-versioned
    siblings outside this same reactor session) is chosen instead.
    -->
    <spring-boot.version>4.1.1</spring-boot.version>
    <!--
    Reverted from 5.1.3 to 5.1.0: io.micronaut.jaxrs:micronaut-jaxrs-server (a separate artifact
    family from core Micronaut, doesn't publish in lockstep with micronaut.platform.version) has
    not published a 5.1.3 release - confirmed directly against Maven Central's metadata, its latest
    is still 5.1.0. Bumping the platform version alone broke dependency resolution for
    agent-os-governance-micronaut. Mixing a newer core-Micronaut version against an older jaxrs
    version was considered and rejected as riskier than staying on the version where everything is
    confirmed in sync.
    -->
    <micronaut.platform.version>5.1.0</micronaut.platform.version>

