  <!--
  Only this repo's own modules - no sibling repos (testcontainers, database-migrations, jpa,
  object-storage, nlp, entity-matching, openworkflow, platform-operations). Those used to be
  listed here directly, but that made this pom BOTH the shared parent every module inherits from
  AND a mega-reactor aggregating the whole ecosystem - and Quarkus's own bootstrap resolver
  (quarkus-bootstrap-maven-resolver, used for quarkus:dev and generate-code-tests) discovers its
  "workspace" by walking up the <parent> chain to the topmost pom and then treats every <module>
  reachable from there as local, reading each one's RAW un-flattened source pom.xml directly
  instead of its properly-flattened, installed artifact. Since every module in every one of these
  repos has this pom as an ancestor, that meant ANY Quarkus module build anywhere in the ecosystem
  could fail on an unrelated sibling repo's un-flattened ${revision} parent reference - confirmed
  live via -X debug output tracing a build failure in forwardmeasure-openworkflow straight back to
  forwardmeasure-jpa's raw source pom, even though the actual, correctly-flattened
  forwardmeasure-jpa-tenancy:1.0.0 artifact was already resolving fine through normal Maven.
  The cross-repo compatibility-verification reactor this used to also serve (see README.md and
  .github/workflows/platform-verify.yml) still exists - it just lives in reactor.xml now, which
  is not anyone's parent, so Quarkus's workspace walk never reaches it.
  -->
  <modules>
